flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the assistant reads the text of an issue
  accDescr: The text of an issue or a comment, which anyone can write, is read up to GitHub's 65,536 characters. The HTML goes first, comments and tags in one pass, with what a video or the brackets of ruby hold, which no browser shows, and with the footnotes where GitHub hides the rest of the text; beside it, from the same text, the cells beyond the header of a table, the source of a diagram, a map or a 3D model and math that can hide text, each with a note in its place, and the title of a link or an image, which the page shows only on hover, with nothing in its place; what either takes out goes. Then the link reference definitions and the footnotes without a reference, which GitHub shows as nothing as well, each with a note in its place, for issue.md and for an excerpt of each other issue, whose form answers then become lines. Then the characters that GitHub shows as nothing go, in one pass, after the HTML, so that none can end an HTML comment that GitHub never ends. The excerpts go into issues.jsonl, and issue.md holds up to 20,000 characters of each text in a code fence that the text can't close. What the assistant decides from the reporter's words, the labels and owners of the area, the reporter's language, the search for older issues and the denial of a fix, it decides from this same shown text, with a space in the place of each note, whose form answers are cut out between their headings, which are found once. Only the box of the opt-out reads the raw text as well: it counts as ticked when it is ticked in the raw or in the shown text.
  text["issue or comment text,<br>which anyone writes"] --> cap["at most 65,536 characters,<br>as much as GitHub keeps"]
  cap --> html["`**strip_html**<br>comments, tags and what<br>a video, an rp or a<br>relative-time holds,<br>in one pass`"]
  cap --> structures["`**structures_of**<br>cells beyond a header,<br>the source of a drawing,<br>math that can hide text,<br>the title of a link`"]
  structures --> definitions
  html --> definitions["`**strip_definitions**<br>link definitions and<br>footnotes without a<br>reference out, a note<br>in the place of each`"]
  definitions --> excerpt["`**excerpt** of every<br>other issue: without HTML,<br>form answers as lines`"]
  definitions --> visible["`**Visible**<br>invisible characters<br>out, in one pass`"]
  excerpt --> visible
  visible -- "the other issues" --> jsonl["`**issues.jsonl**,<br>an excerpt of each`"]
  visible -- "the issue" --> issue["`**issue.md**, up to 20,000<br>characters of each text,<br>each in its own fence`"]
  visible -- "as_shown, a space<br>for each note" --> forms["`**form_fields**<br>each heading found once,<br>answers cut out between`"]
  forms --> event["labels and owners of the area,<br>the reporter's language,<br>the search for older issues,<br>the denial of a fix"]
  cap --> box["box of the opt-out:<br>ticked in the raw<br>or in the shown text"]
  forms --> box
  classDef untrusted fill:#cf222e26,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  class text untrusted
  class cap,forms,excerpt,html,structures,definitions,visible job
  class event,box,jsonl,issue safe
